              "name": "Genetics",
              "description": "Heredity, Mendel's laws, dominant and recessive traits.",
              "estimatedMinutes": 35,
              "lesson": {
                "title": "Introduction to Genetics",
                "introduction": "Genetics is the study of how characteristics are passed from parents to offspring.",
                "explanation": "Each parent passes one allele (version of a gene) for a trait. If the alleles are different, the dominant allele shows in the offspring while the recessive allele is hidden.\n\nExample: In pea plants, tall (T) is dominant over short (t). A cross TT × tt gives all Tt offspring — all tall. A cross Tt × Tt gives TT, Tt, Tt, tt in a 3:1 tall:short ratio.\n\nMendel called the physical appearance the phenotype and the allele pair the genotype (TT, Tt or tt). The Punnett square is a simple grid used to work out offspring genotypes and ratios.",
                "keyPoints": [
                  "Genes come in alleles; dominant vs recessive.",
                  "Genotype = allele pair; phenotype = appearance.",
                  "Mendel's ratios: monohybrid cross gives 3:1.",
                  "Punnett squares predict outcomes."
                ]
              },
              "questions": [
                {
                  "type": "MCQ", "prompt": "In a cross between two heterozygous tall plants (Tt × Tt), what is the phenotypic ratio of tall to short?", "difficulty": 3, "marks": 2,
                  "options": [{"key": "A", "text": "1:1"}, {"key": "B", "text": "3:1"}, {"key": "C", "text": "1:3"}, {"key": "D", "text": "9:3:3:1"}],
                  "correctKey": "B",
                  "explanation": "Tt × Tt gives TT, Tt, Tt, tt — three tall to one short (3:1)."
                },
                {
                  "type": "MCQ", "prompt": "The physical appearance of an organism is its", "difficulty": 1, "marks": 1,
                  "options": [{"key": "A", "text": "genotype"}, {"key": "B", "text": "phenotype"}, {"key": "C", "text": "gene"}, {"key": "D", "text": "chromosome"}],
                  "correctKey": "B",
                  "explanation": "Phenotype = observable appearance; genotype = allele combination."
                },
                {
                  "type": "MCQ", "prompt": "If T is tall (dominant) and t is short (recessive), which genotype is short?", "difficulty": 2, "marks": 1,
                  "options": [{"key": "A", "text": "TT"}, {"key": "B", "text": "Tt"}, {"key": "C", "text": "tt"}, {"key": "D", "text": "Tt and TT"}],
                  "correctKey": "C",
                  "explanation": "Short only appears when both alleles are recessive (tt)."
                }
              ]
            },
